.TH BAN 10 "October 2026" "1.1" "Neverdark Manual"
.SH NAME
ban \- Ban a player from a region
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ban
.I player
.RI [ region ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Ban
.I player
from a region. The banned player is refused entry there but is told which
region refused them; you are told the ban landed, and the victim is told
they were banned.
.PP
The region is a bare world number (0\-65535) or the keyword \fBcosmos\fP,
under exactly the same rules as every other region selector. Without one the
command acts on your \fBdefault target region\fP (see \fBtarget\fP(10)), or
on the region you are standing in if you have set none. Regions at other
widths (districts, super\-planet regions \-\- see \fBgrant\fP(10)) are
reached through your default; see \fBtarget\fP(10) for the width\-and\-point
form.
.PP
You must rule the region, or an ancestor of it, or the command is refused
and names the ruler. The root player cannot be banned, and the victim must
be a player, not a thing.
.PP
A ban bites on arrival, not at login: a banned player who is already
elsewhere may still log in, but cannot enter the region. Login is
deliberately never refused, so a cosmos\-wide ban cannot lock anyone out of
the game entirely.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unban,target,here,planet,deny (10)
.SH AUTHOR
quirinpa <quirinpa@tty.pt>
